WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.652
Calendar files and repeat rules, explained.

2
00:00:05.152 --> 00:00:09.836
What is inside an .ics file, how repeat rules like last Friday of the month

3
00:00:09.836 --> 00:00:14.645
work, and how to turn a spreadsheet or a shift pattern into calendar invites.

4
00:00:16.045 --> 00:00:23.817
What is inside an .ics file. An .ics file is plain text, defined by a standard

5
00:00:23.817 --> 00:00:25.411
called RFC 5545.

6
00:00:26.711 --> 00:00:32.279
Repeat rules, in plain words. The RRULE line packs a lot into a short string.

7
00:00:33.579 --> 00:00:35.563
Merging and cleaning calendars.

8
00:00:35.563 --> 00:00:40.555
If you export calendars from several places, you often end up with duplicates.

9
00:00:41.855 --> 00:00:44.417
Week numbers and other small questions.

10
00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:46.783
Many workplaces plan by week number.

11
00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:51.934
To try it, open Calendar Event Maker (ICS) in OpenFile.

12
00:00:51.934 --> 00:00:55.925
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

13
00:00:55.925 --> 00:00:59.496
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

14
00:01:01.196 --> 00:01:05.143
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
